Linnea for gcsim, from an unmerged gcsim pull request, plus three timing fixes.

Source: https://github.com/genshinsim/gcsim/pull/2596 by TheSast (frames counted by caramielle),
        at commit 0e439a5 (2026-11-10), which is based on gcsim v2.50.0.
Not reviewed or accepted by gcsim's maintainers: results are experimental.

Left out: the website files (ui/) and data_gen.textproto (the reviewers asked for it to be deleted).

Fixes added by this project (gcsim's frame-consistency test failed without them):
  - Skill: the full animation length was a placeholder ("// ?", 14 frames) shorter than the
    measured cancels; it is now the longest measured cancel (aim, 44).
  - Burst: the earliest next action is the skill at 96, not the swap at 97.
  - Normal attack 3: the next attack can't start (43, from before the frames were measured)
    before the measured arrow release (47); it is now 47.

Known open points from gcsim's review (not changed here): how C1 "Field Catalog" stacks are used
up may be wrong (affects C1 and up only); some timings are still estimates.

This file is applied by scripts/build-gcsim.sh. When gcsim includes Linnea itself, the build
skips it and says so; then delete this file.

